From 3f3d6d9557475c1818a2a94347bb5d71263c91da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:08:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(verify): the mid-turn sweep reads the whole turn, not
 five poses

Law (c3) sampled the band stack's column at 4 path stations x 5 turn
fractions; between them a band could cross stock unseen. It now builds
swept cells per band (verify/turn_cells.rs): the hull of law (c)'s
column at a turn interval's two end poses, grown by a proven sag (at
most 0.001 mm until the 64-cell cap), swept exactly along each tip
chord, with the flutes' kerf excused only where the tip stands. The
overhang backstop keeps its sampled grid (#1316).

Pinned by sim midturn_swept_band (clean on main, SweepHit here) and the
brute-force probe verify::turn_cells::tests (5 million band positions,
none outside the cells).

Fixes #1313

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
